MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- #30141 spec: draft-mtp get_state/set_state of the boundary hidden row (pending_h), so context checkpoints restore it
  instead of leaving a stale row of whatever ran last
- #31350 server: a partial acceptance of a draft longer than n_rs_seq restores its checkpoint (n_draft > n_rs_seq,
  the same condition that creates it) instead of only when n_rollback > n_rs_seq. No-op in production
  (n_rs_seq = max(draft n_max, lookup n_max) >= every draft)
- #31368 memory: refuse rollbacks past the snapshots of the last ubatch. Recurrent cells record rs_max (n - 1 for a
  ubatch of n <= n_rs_seq + 1 tokens, else 0); topka applies it to the rollbacks that read snapshot planes only (no
  rs_lag, or no rs_conv_lag); the lagged states stay bounded by rs_pend_n (the replay covers long ubatches). DSV4 cache
  as upstream (update_rs_for_ubatches)
- #30574 server: the slot file ends with the live draft state (full draft context + speculative state, "SDFT"
  appendix after the checkpoints); a draft state that does not fit is dropped, older files keep working. Upstream:
  Qwen MTP acceptance after restore 37% -> 49%. Test test_slot_restore_draft_state ported
